 "9835": {
  "en": [
   "Who has come today, in this deep midnight,",
   "to destroy the peace of the beloved grove?",
   "Like a maddened elephant trampling the lotus beds,",
   "churning the clear lake —",
   "why does he slay the sleeping birds,",
   "aiming sharp arrows again and again?",
   "Startled in terror, stag and doe",
   "flee on stumbling feet.",
   "On stumbling feet they flee through the grove,",
   "gazing with piteous eyes —",
   "the anguished lake, the crane-pair",
   "enter the reed-brake, weeping.",
   "Darkness fills every quarter; the deep night",
   "casts its thick shadow of danger —",
   "the heart rises trembling in terror."
